xecution ability than users or the platform expect, increasing the blast radius if the script or invocation behavior is unsafe.","remediation":"Explicitly declare the minimum required tool scope in the skill metadata, e.g. restrict to the specific shell/tool capability needed for `search.sh`. Also document the exact commands the skill is allowed to run and avoid relying on implicit shell access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1788451dba7b455aa77b351c37807754","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":26,"end_line":29},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill encourages use as a default search tool but does not clearly warn, near the usage guidance, that queries are transmitted to Prismfy and potentially onward to third-party search engines. This creates a privacy and data-handling risk because users may disclose sensitive prompts under the assumption they remain local.","remediation":"Add a prominent disclosure in the description and usage sections that all search queries are sent to Prismfy and may be processed by selected external engines. Recommend that users avoid submitting secrets, personal data, or confidential internal information.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":26,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-36a3a126ba5d41ef9bb61f0cc1a37a89","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":null},"finding":"create a free account, and grab your API key from **Dashboard → API Keys**.\nNo credit card required.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Add the key to your environment\n\n**Option A — Shell profile (permanent)**\n```bash\n# Ad","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n### 2. Get an API key\n\nHead to [prismfy.io](https://prismfy.io), create a free account, and grab your API key from **Dashboard → API Keys**.\nNo credit card required.\n\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2ed9d1ade684159a06dd83041ee2b6bd3ecb895a558bc455f26ee0f90cf08615","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-d3ad994d0e234c8f80400ada365af0b6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null},"finding":"Add to ~/.zshrc","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n**Option A — Shell profile (permanent)**\n```bash\n# Add to ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc:\nexport PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"\n\n# Then reload:","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cbe14530e4c3cd37b89b245a138ef751f4b9bc407f3b0e44b077af50a89f7e4d","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-4541c445d8a8429381d1c58cbb20f421","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":99},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language examples are very broad and resemble ordinary conversation, which can cause the skill to trigger when a user is merely discussing a topic rather than intentionally invoking web search. In a default-search skill, that ambiguity can silently send user prompts to an external provider and execute shell commands without clear user intent.","remediation":"Narrow the invocation patterns so they are clearly command-like, or require an explicit trigger such as `/search`. Add wording that natural-language activation sends the request to an external provider and should only occur when the user is clearly asking to search.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-7262753b7ca34f068934a482fcbf69d1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"hooks/openclaw/HOOK.md","start_line":33,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The hook registers on every agent bootstrap and instructs the agent to prefer live search whenever information might be current, with broad categories like library docs, code examples, community opinions, and pricing. This can cause the tool to be invoked far more often than necessary, increasing external data exposure, quota consumption, and the chance that untrusted web content influences downstream responses.","remediation":"Narrow the activation guidance to explicit user requests or clearly defined triggers, rather than broad default preference language. Add constraints such as requiring user consent for web access, limiting auto-use to time-sensitive queries only, and documenting trust boundaries for search results so the agent does not over-rely on external content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"hooks/openclaw/HOOK.md","start_line":33,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9765cd5c4ef740c0851a5d7aa8eb3ab6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"search.sh","start_line":153,"end_line":154},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script sends the user's search query and optional filters such as domain, language, page, and engine selection to the remote Prismfy API, but it does not clearly warn the user at execution time that their input will leave the local environment. In a search skill this data flow is expected, but the lack of explicit disclosure can still create a privacy issue if users enter sensitive terms assuming a local-only tool.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing notice in the help text and first-run/runtime output stating that queries and filters are transmitted to Prismfy's remote service. Also document what fields are sent, avoid encouraging entry of secrets, and consider an explicit consent flag or configuration option for environments with stricter privacy requirements.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"search.sh","start_line":153,"end_line":154}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2447,"completion_tokens":264,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2711},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2126,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2140},{"node":"s